      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-9963",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $8 \\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\textrm{rank}(A)=5$ then what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then  \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) + \\textrm{nullity}(A) = n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
